from pathlib import Path
import json, html
import markdown
OUT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
ROOT=OUT.parents[3]
def figure(name, caption, cls=''):
    return f'<figure class="{cls}"><a href="{name}"><img loading="lazy" src="{name}" alt="{html.escape(caption)}"></a><figcaption>{caption}</figcaption></figure>'
def receipt(name):
    path=OUT/name
    if not path.exists(): return 'pending'
    obj=json.loads(path.read_text())
    return (str(len(obj.get('checks',[])))+' passed') if obj.get('passed') and obj.get('checks') else ('passed' if obj.get('passed') else 'failed')
reading=markdown.markdown((ROOT/'commons/maps/Point_Lines/final.void.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8'),extensions=['footnotes','tables'])
rows=[('Arrival','One room, two points, one segment. Move an endpoint; see its length and direction change.'),('Connections','The west wing opens the pair into a field of points. Connect, then move them apart.'),('Directions','Blue wooden police barricades, a walking stripe and a red boundary give the line different force.'),('A body','The eye follows a line into empty air. Fixed timber carries the player over the shaft.'),('Relations','Loose sticks make parallel lines, a plus and an X. The original pickups remain available.'),('Consequences','The X and recovery plus now sit beyond the workbench. They act on the same tower health system.')]
route=''.join(f'<li><b>{title}</b><p>{body}</p></li>' for title,body in rows)
gallery=figure('lines-arrival.png','Arrival: unfinished partitions screen the later examples. Enter the original two-point room.')+figure('lines-measure.png','First encounter: two movable endpoints, their segment and the existing measurement. Real Godot capture.')
gallery+=figure('lines-directions.png','Later: the blue painted wooden barricades. Supply cables now run overhead, leaving floor markings to the artifacts.')+figure('lines-bridge.png','The line acquires a body. Reused plank geometry and its collider carry the crossing.')+figure('lines-health.png','The health pair follows the construction studies, with a clear approach and a way around it.')+figure('lines-timber.png','The workbench retains its original loose examples. This is the next area to refine by editing the shared plan.')
body=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The Void / a route we can edit</title><style>
:root{{--paper:#f3efe7;--ink:#272731;--muted:#67636b;--rose:#b96686;--line:#d5ccc5}}*{{box-sizing:border-box}}body{{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}}main{{max-width:1220px;margin:auto;padding:40px 32px 100px}}header{{max-width:900px;padding:30px 0}}.eyebrow{{font:12px/1.5 monospace;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--rose)}}h1{{font:clamp(40px,6vw,78px)/1.03 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:22px 0}}h2{{font:36px/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:58px 0 20px}}h3{{font-size:20px}}p{{max-width:76ch}}.lead{{font-size:22px}}a{{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:4px}}nav{{display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:18px 0;border-block:1px solid var(--line)}}figure{{margin:0 0 26px}}img{{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;background:#1a222d;border-radius:3px}}figcaption{{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);padding:12px 0}}.grid{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:26px}}.route{{counter-reset:route;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:26px;padding:0;list-style:none}}.route li{{border-top:2px solid var(--rose);padding:16px 0}}.route li:before{{counter-increment:route;content:counter(route,decimal-leading-zero);display:block;font:13px monospace;color:var(--rose);margin-bottom:10px}}.route p{{font-size:15px}}.note{{border-left:3px solid var(--rose);padding:12px 24px;background:#eae2dc}}.steps{{max-width:850px}}.steps li{{margin:12px 0}}code{{font-size:.88em;background:#e7e0da;padding:2px 5px}}table{{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:15px}}td,th{{text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:12px}}article{{max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;font:20px/1.8 Georgia,serif}}article h1{{font-size:46px}}article h2{{font-size:30px}}article a{{overflow-wrap:anywhere}}details{{margin:22px 0}}summary{{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}}footer{{margin-top:60px;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}}@media(max-width:760px){{main{{padding:20px}}.grid,.route{{grid-template-columns:1fr}}}}
</style></head><body><main><header><div class="eyebrow">Ada Research · The Void · 18 October 2026</div><h1>A route we can edit.</h1><p class="lead">One line first. Then what a line can do.</p><p>The floor is the space of the artifacts. Electrical distribution moves to 4.8 metres above it; unfinished partitions make a first encounter before the wider collection opens.</p></header><nav><a href="#route">The encounter order</a><a href="#editor">Edit it in Godot</a><a href="#before">Before / after</a><a href="#museum">Inside the tower</a><a href="#checks">Verification</a><a href="#reading">Tower reading</a></nav>
{figure('lines-measure.png','The original two-point artifact is now the first encounter on Floor 03.')}
<section id="route"><h2>Give each encounter room.</h2><ol class="route">{route}</ol><p>The order is a proposal recorded in the layout. It can change. The shafts and pillars stay fixed; partitions, props, assemblies and individual examples can move.</p></section>
<section id="editor"><h2>Your edits become the floor.</h2>{figure('native-editor.png','Native Godot editor. Beige: partitions and pillars. Pink outlines: actual artifact geometry. Green: the proposed route.')}
<p>Reopen this Godot project and click <b>Void Floors</b> in the bottom panel. Expand the panel for more room. If it is not visible, enable it under <b>Project Settings → Plugins → Void Floors</b>.</p><ol class="steps"><li>Choose a floor. Select an assembly or an individual part in the plan or searchable list.</li><li>Drag it on the grid, enter X/Z coordinates, or rotate it by 90°. Undo and Redo retain the whole layout.</li><li>Draw an unfinished wall with two clicks. Set its height. Place a pallet, fence, concrete barrier, crate or full-size shipping container.</li><li>Use <b>Walk this floor</b> to launch the real desktop scene from your unsaved draft.</li><li><b>Save layout</b> updates the file used by the normal VR game and web editor. Restart the Void scene or reload the web editor to see the change.</li></ol><p><a href="/book-review/addons/void_floor_editor/README.md">Editor guide</a> · <a href="http://localhost:3003/editor/void">Shared web editor</a> · <a href="/book-review/commons/void/rooms.json">Current layout</a></p><div class="note"><b>One authored layout.</b> Both editors use <code>commons/void/rooms.json</code>. Native saves validate placements, keep a backup and reject a revision changed elsewhere. The floor structure remains in <code>layout.json</code>; original artifact behavior stays in its scenes.</div><p>Existing project prefabs supply the pallet, temporary fence and concrete barrier. These are procedural project assets, not the photographed asset pack in the references. The palette is deliberately small.</p></section>
<section id="before"><h2>Before / after.</h2><div class="grid">{figure('../2026-10-18-void-point-lines/lines-directions.png','Previous open arrangement: teaching examples and service lines share the floor. Earlier capture from a different position.')}{figure('lines-directions.png','Revised arrangement: overhead services and unfinished partitions give the artifacts clearer surroundings.')}</div><p>The original museum <code>final.md</code> is preserved. The tower adaptation changes its opening order: first the two-point room, then the field of points. The reflective passages remain available.</p></section>
<section id="museum"><h2>Inside the tower.</h2><div class="grid">{gallery}</div><details><summary>Mobile renderer view</summary>{figure('mobile/lines-directions.png','Godot Mobile renderer on the desktop GPU. This verifies rendering, not physical headset performance.')}</details></section>
<section id="checks"><h2>What has been checked.</h2><table><tr><th>Check</th><th>Result</th></tr><tr><td>Desktop and synthetic XR movement, interactions, health and recovery</td><td>{receipt('checks.json')}</td></tr><tr><td>Packaged game using Android resource exclusions</td><td>{receipt('package-checks.json')}</td></tr><tr><td>Native editor editing and undo/redo</td><td>{receipt('native-editor-checks.json')}</td></tr><tr><td>Revision checks, backups and invalid placements</td><td>{receipt('editor-save-checks.json')}</td></tr><tr><td>Native editor draft loaded by the real game</td><td>{receipt('editor-runtime-checks.json')}</td></tr><tr><td>Shared web editor validation and save/reload</td><td>{receipt('editor-checks.json')}</td></tr></table><p>Tests walk through the new entrance, its side opening and the west passage, and over the timber crossing. The VR relocation fix lets XRTools find the runtime-created player body when resetting its position.</p><p>The changed web-editor page has no TypeScript diagnostics. The wider encyclopedia still reports 288 diagnostics in other files; this pass does not claim a clean full-project typecheck.</p><p>Physical headset comfort and performance remain untested. Placement validation cannot guarantee every route after arbitrary part edits. Use the walk preview and test the saved arrangement in VR. The east workbench still has many variants; it is a useful next place to judge pacing together.</p><p><a href="receipt.json">Game receipt</a> · <a href="physics.log">Native log</a> · <a href="native-editor-checks.json">Editor checks</a> · <a href="editor-runtime-checks.json">Editor → game check</a></p></section>
<section id="reading"><h2>The tower reading.</h2><article>{reading}</article></section><footer>Images are captured from the running Godot scene. The green editorial route is visible in the editors; it is not painted over the artifacts in VR.</footer></main></body></html>'''
(OUT/'index.html').write_text(body,encoding='utf-8')
